==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Disciple Psychoduck''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Malevolent Mad-Duck''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Bunny & Canard shares the same strengths and weaknesses with the original, being a powerful Target Only specialist backliner held back by his sluggish attack rate, high cost and low speed. He works best against enemies he can outrange with few knockbacks in general, though in many cases he won't last long without support.

==='''Normal Form'''===
This form seems to be the most useful on paper given the prevalence of Red and Dark threats. While he can dominate most Reds without trouble, many common Darks can be easily staggered by small amounts of damage from other units brought to fight them, causing him to miss. This weakens his compatibility and mostly restricts him to fighting the likes of [[Le'noir]] and [[Razorback]], which don't tend to stagger from weak attacks.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Disciple Psychoduck's niche remains the same against Reds, but isn't that great against most zombies due to their burrowing ability. Due to his slow attack rate and extremely long foreswing, he can miss dangerous zombies that have burrowed recently, and is essentially defenseless if they resurface on him, having to rely on other competent support units to repel them. However, he can still be of use, as he easily outranges most common zombies, notably [[Cadaver Bear]], and can deal heavy damage to them if he does hit.

==='''True Form'''===
Malevolent Mad-Duck now targets [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies. His anti-Red performance is the same. On the one hand, he can deal immense damage to any Akus he hits. On the other hand, he lacks [[Shield Piercing|Shield Piercer]], which limits his usability against Aku enemies or has him rely on other units to pierce shields where he can't just use brute force to beat them.

However, Malevolent Mad-Duck also enjoys two new buffs: Surge Immunity and Toxic Immunity.

Surge Immunity helps against [[Sinner Snache]], [[Raynard]], [[Condemned Peng]], [[Wicked Tank Cat (Enemy)|Wicked Tank Cat]], [[Red EnerG]], [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]] and [[Medu-san]]. All of these enemies are threats primarily because of their surges. Additionally, none of them have shields, so Malevolent Mad-Duck can use his powerful offenses on them uninhibited. This ability also helps against [[Lord of Ruin Jagando]]'s invasion stage, as Condemned Pengs, Fallen Bears and Jagando himself are notorious for spawning many surge attacks.

Toxic Immunity, on the other hand, is only really helpful against [[High Priest Mamon]] and [[Infernal Tyrant Nyandam]] as no other enemies with the Toxic ability have a trait that Malevolent Mad-Duck can actually attack. This can help on some mixed stages, but as a target only unit, he shines in few of those.

